.policy "ruff-c403-unnecessary-list-comprehension-set" revision 2
.description "Use a set comprehension instead of passing a list comprehension to set; it skips building a throwaway list."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff C403 (flake8-comprehensions): `set(…)` of the builtin set, whose one argument is a list
// comprehension. Its fix is unsafe; none here.
//   set([f(x) for x in y])     ← C403: {f(x) for x in y}
//   set([x for x in y], z)     not reported
#include "python/comprehensions.rr"
//   c4_call(c, x), c4_only(c, a), c4_comp(e, k)

.violation C403(at: node) code "C403"
    "Rewrite `set([expr for ...])` as a set comprehension `{{expr for ...}}`; the intermediate list is not needed."
    suppress ruff "C403"
C403(c) :- c4_call(c, "set"), c4_only(c, l), c4_comp(l, "list").
